## English summary

**{{APP_NAME_EN}}** is a teaching demo ({{SERIES_NAME_EN}}) by {{AUTHOR}}, {{UNIVERSITY_EN}}. One idea goes through a
controllable 9-agent workflow (idea, script, review & compliance, characters, storyboard, director board, art, compose,
quality check) that reads and writes one shared structured state, with checkpoints and re-runs from any stage. The
browser version (`play/index.html`, double-click, offline; also laid out for phones in portrait) is a line-by-line
JavaScript port of the Python pipeline's deterministic mock mode — verified field by field against Python on
{{PARITY_CASES}} idea/seed/preset cases — and shows a live pipeline panel, a character-consistency matrix, cost presets
with multi-model dispatch, and a 3D director stage (three.js r128). Text is rule-generated and images are placeholders:
it demonstrates the engineering loop, not output quality. Code: MIT; docs: CC BY 4.0.
